     - Atmospheric nuclear weapon testing;
     - Service at Hiroshima or Nagasaki during the occupation;
     - Was a prisoner of war (POW) held for more than 150 days in Japan before and after being released;
     - Worked as an x-ray technician, radiographer, nuclear medicine technologist, or worked near/operated with a nuclear weapon facility while on active duty or during qualifying inactive training (R&R);

